.TH SKEWER-SHELL-SCRIPTING 1
.SH NAME
skewer-shell-scripting \- working and scripting in a Skewer session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skewer shell
.br
.B skewer run -- PROGRAM [ARGUMENTS...]
.br
.B skewer status | env | check
.RI [ --json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Skewer retains your normal shell and adds a routed cgroup, a process guard,
session variables and, for Bash, a status marker. It is not a container.
Closing the GUI does not disable routing or stop applications.
.SH COMMANDS
.B attach PID... [--cleanup|--no-cleanup] [--yes]
attaches explicitly selected processes. Cleanup defaults to the shared GUI
setting (off initially). Children are not implicitly selected by this command.
.PP
.B cleanup PID... [--dry-run] [--yes]
closes existing TCP sockets outside Skewer for the specified attached processes.
Requires privilege authorization. The helper verifies UID, process start time,
current membership, socket ownership and kernel cookie. UDP and listeners are
untouched. --dry-run only reports eligible sockets. Scripts require --yes for
destructive cleanup; interactive sessions ask for confirmation.
Transfers may be interrupted and applications are NOT guaranteed to reconnect.
.PP
.B status
reports a fresh observation of the calling process cgroup, policy route
and configured Saslik API. It does not read the prompt's cached status.
.PP
.B env
lists public session variables. Output is informational, not shell source;
do not eval it. Use --json for machine-readable output.
.PP
.B check
performs the same control-plane checks and exits 0 for an active route
(with API availability when configured), 1 for an unavailable or unknown
state, and 2 for invalid arguments. --require-routed explicitly requests
this default behavior. This is NOT an end-to-end traffic test.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
skewer check --require-routed || exit 1
curl https://example.com
.fi
.PP
Launch the script with skewer run -- ./script.sh, or from skewer shell.
A successful check does not guarantee the route will remain available.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
SKEWER_SESSION identifies a session. SKEWER_CGROUP is its original cgroup.
SKEWER_GATEWAY and SKEWER_API_URL describe configuration at launch time.
SKEWER_CA_FILE names the selected runtime CA, if configured.
These variables are not live health indicators. No API credentials are exported.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Existing sockets retain their original routing association. The guard
repairs the root process throughout its lifetime and newly discovered
descendants for five seconds. Polling is not leak prevention: an application
can create a socket before repair. IPv6 and destination exemptions may
bypass the IPv4 route. The prompt is a cached control-plane indication,
not proof of interception. Use an actual traffic test for that.
.SH HELP
man skewer-shell-scripting
